\f0\b\fs24 \cf2 \cb3 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 # Cellalyze
\f1\b0 \cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \cb3 Cellalyze is a learning project for exploring single-cell RNA sequencing data in a browser. It uses Streamlit for the interface and Scanpy for basic single-cell analysis.\cb1 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 ## Current Features
\f1\b0 \cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \cb3 For AnnData \cf2 \strokec2 `.h5ad`\cf4 \strokec4  files, the app currently:\cb1 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf5 \cb3 \strokec5 -\cf4 \strokec4  Loads an uploaded dataset.\cb1 \
\cf5 \cb3 \strokec5 -\cf4 \strokec4  Reports basic dataset information, including cell and gene counts.\cb1 \
\cf5 \cb3 \strokec5 -\cf4 \strokec4  Normalizes counts to a target sum of 10,000 per cell.\cb1 \
\cf5 \cb3 \strokec5 -\cf4 \strokec4  Applies \cf2 \strokec2 `log1p`\cf4 \strokec4  transformation.\cb1 \
\cf5 \cb3 \strokec5 -\cf4 \strokec4  Selects up to 2,000 highly variable genes.\cb1 \
\cf5 \cb3 \strokec5 -\cf4 \strokec4  Computes PCA and a nearest-neighbor graph.\cb1 \
\cf5 \cb3 \strokec5 -\cf4 \strokec4  Attempts Leiden clustering and stores the result as \cf2 \strokec2 `clusters`\cf4 \strokec4 .\cb1 \
\cf5 \cb3 \strokec5 -\cf4 \strokec4  Computes a UMAP embedding.\cb1 \
\cf5 \cb3 \strokec5 -\cf4 \strokec4  Displays interactive Plotly UMAP visualizations.\cb1 \
\cf5 \cb3 \strokec5 -\cf4 \strokec4  Colors UMAP cells by gene expression or cell metadata.\cb1 \
\cf5 \cb3 \strokec5 -\cf4 \strokec4  Displays a Scanpy UMAP plot for the selected feature.\cb1 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \cb3 CSV and CSV.GZ files are currently supported as tabular previews. They can be inspected and plotted by column, but they are not yet converted into AnnData or processed through the single-cell workflow.\cb1 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 ## Tech Stack
\f1\b0 \cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf5 \cb3 \strokec5 -\cf4 \strokec4  Python\cb1 \
\cf5 \cb3 \strokec5 -\cf4 \strokec4  Streamlit\cb1 \
\cf5 \cb3 \strokec5 -\cf4 \strokec4  Scanpy and AnnData\cb1 \
\cf5 \cb3 \strokec5 -\cf4 \strokec4  pandas\cb1 \
\cf5 \cb3 \strokec5 -\cf4 \strokec4  NumPy\cb1 \
\cf5 \cb3 \strokec5 -\cf4 \strokec4  Matplotlib\cb1 \
\cf5 \cb3 \strokec5 -\cf4 \strokec4  Plotly\cb1 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 ## Setup
\f1\b0 \cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \cb3 Use Python 3.10 or newer. From the project directory, create a virtual environment and install the dependencies:\cb1 \
\
\cb3 ```bash\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf6 \cb3 \strokec6 cd\cf4 \strokec7  \cf8 \strokec8 /Users/chloeyfang/scRNAseq-visualizer\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf5 \cb3 \strokec5 python3\cf4 \strokec7  \cf9 \strokec9 -m\cf4 \strokec7  \cf8 \strokec8 venv\cf4 \strokec7  \cf8 \strokec8 venv\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf6 \cb3 \strokec6 source\cf4 \strokec7  \cf8 \strokec8 venv/bin/activate\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf5 \cb3 \strokec5 python\cf4 \strokec7  \cf9 \strokec9 -m\cf4 \strokec7  \cf8 \strokec8 pip\cf4 \strokec7  \cf8 \strokec8 install\cf4 \strokec7  \cf9 \strokec9 --upgrade\cf4 \strokec7  \cf8 \strokec8 pip\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\cf5 \cb3 \strokec5 python\cf4 \strokec7  \cf9 \strokec9 -m\cf4 \strokec7  \cf8 \strokec8 pip\cf4 \strokec7  \cf8 \strokec8 install\cf4 \strokec7  \cf8 \strokec8 streamlit\cf4 \strokec7  \cf8 \strokec8 scanpy\cf4 \strokec7  \cf8 \strokec8 pandas\cf4 \strokec7  \cf8 \strokec8 numpy\cf4 \strokec7  \cf8 \strokec8 matplotlib\cf4 \strokec7  \cf8 \strokec8 plotly\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \cb3 ```\cb1 \
\
\cb3 The existing \cf2 \strokec2 `venv312`\cf4 \strokec4  directory may point to a Python installation that is no longer present. Creating a fresh \cf2 \strokec2 `venv`\cf4 \strokec4  as shown above avoids that broken interpreter reference.\cb1 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 ## Run the App
\f1\b0 \cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \cb3 From the project directory, with the virtual environment activated:\cb1 \
\
\cb3 ```bash\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf5 \cb3 \strokec5 streamlit\cf4 \strokec7  \cf8 \strokec8 run\cf4 \strokec7  \cf8 \strokec8 app.py\cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \cb3 ```\cb1 \
\
\cb3 Streamlit will print a local URL, normally:\cb1 \
\
\cb3 ```text\cb1 \
\cb3 http://localhost:8501\cb1 \
\cb3 ```\cb1 \
\
\cb3 Stop the app with \cf2 \strokec2 `Ctrl+C`\cf4 \strokec4  in the terminal.\cb1 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 ## Using the App
\f1\b0 \cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf5 \cb3 \strokec5 1.\cf4 \strokec4  Open the local Streamlit URL in a browser.\cb1 \
\cf5 \cb3 \strokec5 2.\cf4 \strokec4  Upload an \cf2 \strokec2 `.h5ad`\cf4 \strokec4  file from the sidebar.\cb1 \
\cf5 \cb3 \strokec5 3.\cf4 \strokec4  Wait for preprocessing and UMAP calculation to finish.\cb1 \
\cf5 \cb3 \strokec5 4.\cf4 \strokec4  Choose whether to color the UMAP by gene expression or cell metadata.\cb1 \
\cf5 \cb3 \strokec5 5.\cf4 \strokec4  Select a gene or metadata column to explore.\cb1 \
\cf5 \cb3 \strokec5 6.\cf4 \strokec4  Inspect the interactive plot and dataset summary.\cb1 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \cb3 A useful starter dataset should contain:\cb1 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf5 \cb3 \strokec5 -\cf4 \strokec4  An expression matrix in \cf2 \strokec2 `adata.X`\cf4 \strokec4 .\cb1 \
\cf5 \cb3 \strokec5 -\cf4 \strokec4  Gene names in \cf2 \strokec2 `adata.var_names`\cf4 \strokec4 .\cb1 \
\cf5 \cb3 \strokec5 -\cf4 \strokec4  Cell names in \cf2 \strokec2 `adata.obs_names`\cf4 \strokec4 .\cb1 \
\cf5 \cb3 \strokec5 -\cf4 \strokec4  Optional cell annotations in \cf2 \strokec2 `adata.obs`\cf4 \strokec4 .\cb1 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 ## Analysis Pipeline
\f1\b0 \cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \cb3 The current H5AD workflow is:\cb1 \
\
\cb3 ```text\cb1 \
\cb3 uploaded H5AD\cb1 \
\cb3     -> normalize total counts\cb1 \
\cb3     -> log1p transform\cb1 \
\cb3     -> highly variable gene selection\cb1 \
\cb3     -> PCA\cb1 \
\cb3     -> neighbor graph\cb1 \
\cb3     -> Leiden clusters\cb1 \
\cb3     -> UMAP\cb1 \
\cb3     -> interactive visualization\cb1 \
\cb3 ```\cb1 \
\
\cb3 The original uploaded object is kept separate from the processed copy so the displayed raw-data summary is not replaced by the normalized values.\cb1 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

